atically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1233,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[2045,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[2046,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[2044,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[966,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[1093,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[540,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[708,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[707,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[445,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1141,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1243,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1403,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1242,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1402,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1803,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[214,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` lets each Card toggle on its own. CardSelectionIndicator shows the\nstate, and its children can render custom content from it. Nested buttons keep their own presses."],[1802,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[215,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` keeps one Card selected at a time. Arrow keys move between Cards, and\nSpace selects the focused one."],[924,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1646,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1689,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[1030,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1740,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[808,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[958,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[764,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."],[2102,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[1424,"`sm`, `md`, or `lg` for the adopted components inside (listed below): their text, controls, and\ndefault spacing."],[95,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1532,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[1180,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[93,"`Tab`"],[538,"`Tab`"],[567,"`Tab`"],[838,"`Tab`"],[962,"`Tab`"],[1849,"`Tab`"],[58,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[491,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[1579,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1576,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1580,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."],[1578,"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."],[1644,"`Text` applies the body role and `Detail` the detail role, each at the tier of the nearest\n`SizeProvider`, or `md` outside any scope."],[1643,"`Text` is body copy and `Detail` is supporting copy: captions, metadata, and hints."],[1664,"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."],[1694,"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1300,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[999,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1840,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[2037,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[1000,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[2047,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[2025,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1903,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[2030,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[2021,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[2105,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[2023,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[2031,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[2034,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[2101,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1904,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[2027,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[2024,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[2022,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[2032,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1940,"✅ Custom domains"],[1941,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1537,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1807,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. Undo / Redo, Zoom In / Out / Reset)"],[1806,"✅ For grouped contextual actions — two or more closely related actions that belong together (e.g. Bold / Italic / Underline, Align Left / Center / Right)"],[1808,"✅ For multi-select scenarios — when users need to select multiple options simultaneously"],[348,"✅ For selecting multiple independent options"],[1536,"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"],[350,"✅ For toggling settings or features on/off"],[1939,"✅ Interactive tooltips"],[1938,"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"],[1936,"✅ Single and multi-series support"],[1937,"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"],[351,"✅ When all available options should be visible"],[1249,"✅ When all options should be visible at once"],[1250,"✅ When the decision is important and deserves space"],[1248,"✅ When there are 2-7 mutually exclusive options"],[349,"✅ When users can select zero, one, or many items"],[1252,"❌ For binary yes/no choices (use Checkbox or Toggle instead)"],[1539,"❌ For choosing one of several mutually exclusive options (use `Radio` or `SegmentedController` instead)"],[1810,"❌ For more than 5 choices — cognitive overload; consider a **Select** instead"],[1251,"❌ For more than 7 options (use Select instead)"],[1813,"❌ For mutually exclusive content views (e.g. Monthly / Yearly) — use **SegmentedController** instead"],[352,"❌ For mutually exclusive options (use Radio instead)"],[1538,"❌ For selections that require a \"Save\" or \"Submit\" action (use `Checkbox` instead)"],[353,"❌ For simple on/off toggles without labels (use Toggle/Switch instead)"],[1809,"❌ For unrelated actions that perform disconnected tasks without shared context"],[1811,"❌ When actions require strong visual distinction (e.g. Save vs. Delete)"],[1812,"❌ When selecting an option leads to a different page or workflow — use navigation instead"],[1253,"❌ When space is limited (use Select dropdown)"],[1944,"🚧 Additional customization options (tick formatting, axis configuration)"],[1942,"🚧 RTL compatibility (axis rendering and spacing refinement)"],[1943,"🚧 Tick mark positioning improvements"],[840,"A `<Button slot=\"trigger\">` gets `aria-expanded` + `aria-controls` wired to the `InlineDrawerPanel` automatically (via RAC Disclosure)."],[225,"A `CardGroup` does not submit form values. Read the selection from `onSelectionChange`."],[221,"A `CardGroup` is a grid: each Card is a row, Tab moves into and out of the group, and arrow keys\nmove between Cards. Name the group with `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Each Card takes its\naccessible name from `textValue`, which also drives typeahead. Plain-text children supply it by\ndefault, so set `textValue` when a Card's content is composed."],[541,"A `Heading slot=\"title\"` labels the dialog via `aria-labelledby`; otherwise pass `aria-label`"],[1094,"A `Heading slot=\"title\"` labels the dialog via `aria-labelledby`. Without one, a popover inside\na `PopoverTrigger` falls back to being labelled by its trigger; standing alone with\n`triggerRef` it needs an explicit `aria-label`"],[922,"A `Menu` is a collection, so it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger` children. Rich content inside a `Menu`\nor submenu is not supported. To show a `Calendar`, let the item close the\nmenu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored to the trigger\n